--TEST--
A property default that is not a literal of the property's own declared type does not compile — `rule:types/declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The default is evaluated once, at compile time, into the constant every
// fresh instance's slot is written with (`nvs_types::defaults`), so it has to
// be a literal of the declared type. Before this was checked, `= "no"` on an
// `int` compiled and the slot read back `0`.
class Bad
{
    public int $n = "no";
    public string $s = 1;

    public function constructor() {}
}

var $b = new Bad();
echo $b->n, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0472]: a property default must be a `int` constant
%A
error[E0472]: a property default must be a `string` constant
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
